				9
			],
			"Message": "docs(Land): Split FilesystemFootprint into index + 6 sub-documents\n\nThe monolithic 500+ line FilesystemFootprint.md was hard to navigate and kept growing unmanageably. Restructure it as a ~100 line index with cross-platform badges, an ownership-domain table, the bundle-identifier story, updated cross-cutting observations (adding two-install-root, two-machine-identity, Air uppercase divergence), and a document index pointing to six focused sub-documents:\n\n- **UserDotfile.md** — the `~/.fiddee/` tree, sub-directory map, Cocoon-side TypeScript mirror, legacy `~/.land/` fan-out, and open questions.\n- **PlatformPaths.md** — OS-specific resolution tables for per-bundle (app_data_dir/cache/log/config), OS-managed (WebKit, plist, SavedState), temp-dir, foreign-tool, and in-tree build paths across macOS, Linux, and Windows.\n- **PerElement.md** — per-Element write-site matrix answering \"where does this Element write?\" (reverse map of the other documents), with the at-a-glance grid.\n- **EnvironmentVariables.md** — every path-shaping env var grouped by role (path overrides, log control, bundle-identifier builders, telemetry localStorage, Sky workbench gates, tier flags) with reader source-file references and defaults.\n- **Cleanup.md** — per-OS complete-wipe recipes (macOS production-validated, Linux XDG-aware, Windows PowerShell forward-looking), archive pattern from the 2026-05-26 cleanup, safety preamble, and a preservation/exclusion table.\n- **Encapsulation.md** — 11 encapsulation directions (A-K) with effort/impact/risk ratings, sequencing suggestion, and versioning sketch, replacing the old \"potential expansion\" section.\n\nUpdate the README.md document index row to reflect the new structure (200+ index + 6 sub-docs). Advance the Element submodule to rebuild Cocoon Target bundles with no new RPC methods (count stays at 140) and correct the Common trait doc comment for ProvideInlineCompletionItems.\n\nThe doc is now navigable by task: cleanup engineers go to Cleanup.md, platform porters go to PlatformPaths.md, versioning planners go to Encapsulation.md.",
